<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 76,028 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 76,028 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 76,028 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 82,055 tonnes in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			11,768	   11,320</p>
<p>    Import cargo			64,260	   70,735</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and four berthed. In the next 24 hours, five ships were expected to sail and 10 were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship	    Berthing</p>
<p>Sugar		    13,125	 Harmony Breeze    15/1</p>
<p>Soyabean oil	   13,000	 Cielo-di-Milano   18/1</p>
<p>Furnace oil	    25,000	 Miraj		 15/1</p>
<p>Sugar		     1,330	 Windco Mariner     due</p>
<p>Crude oil		73,000	 Johar		 12/1</p>
<p>Chemical		  7,500	 Bakri Orbitor	8/1</p>
<p>High speed deisel    75,000	 Chesapeak City     due</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
